    "content": "Anxiety has become one of the most common emotional struggles of modern life. The mind keeps moving from one thought to another, often worrying about situations that have not even happened yet. Questions such as “What if I fail?”, “What if something goes wrong?”, or “What if I am not able to handle the future?” can repeat themselves so often that they begin to disturb our peace. If you are searching for how to control anxiety , the first thing to understand is that anxiety is not always created by the situation itself. Very often, it is created by the way the mind repeatedly interprets, predicts and reacts to that situation. This is also why people who want to know how to calm your mind often discover that simply telling themselves to “stop thinking” does not work. The Bhagavad Gita offers a deeper approach. Instead of asking us to suppress thoughts, it teaches us how to understand the mind, observe it, train it and act with greater awareness. The Gita does not promise a life without c...",
    "contentHtml": "<p>Anxiety has become one of the most common emotional struggles of modern life. The mind keeps moving from one thought to another, often worrying about situations that have not even happened yet. Questions such as “What if I fail?”, “What if something goes wrong?”, or “What if I am not able to handle the future?” can repeat themselves so often that they begin to disturb our peace.</p><p>If you are searching for <strong>how to control anxiety</strong>, the first thing to understand is that anxiety is not always created by the situation itself. Very often, it is created by the way the mind repeatedly interprets, predicts and reacts to that situation. This is also why people who want to know <strong>how to calm your mind</strong> often discover that simply telling themselves to “stop thinking” does not work.</p><p>The Bhagavad Gita offers a deeper approach. Instead of asking us to suppress thoughts, it teaches us how to understand the mind, observe it, train it and act with greater awareness. The Gita does not promise a life without challenges. Instead, it teaches us how to remain inwardly steady even when life outside remains uncertain.</p><p>This is also the essence of the <strong>Living the Gita Movement</strong>. The purpose is not merely to read the Bhagavad Gita or admire its teachings, but to bring those teachings into everyday life. When fear appears, when the mind becomes restless, when expectations create pressure, or when uncertainty makes us anxious, that is precisely when the Gita needs to be lived.</p><p></p><p><img alt=\"Meditating with Bhagavad Gita for anxiety relief and inner peace.\" fetchPriority=\"high\" width=\"1588\" height=\"893\" decoding=\"async\" data-nimg=\"1\" class=\"rounded-lg md:mx-auto lg:mx-auto  xl:mx-auto\" style=\"color:transparent\" sizes=\"100vw\" srcSet=\"https://cdn.typeflo.io/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fauth.typeflo.io%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Fposts%2Fpublic%2F6eae6931-f95c-4bcd-b740-e9c3acce8146%2F45ec8a3c-1a2a-4e55-9148-955458ca2eb3%2Fqjse5gp.webp%3F1789031992453&amp;w=640&amp;q=75 640w, https://cdn.typeflo.io/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fauth.typeflo.io%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Fposts%2Fpublic%2F6eae6931-f95c-4bcd-b740-e9c3acce8146%2F45ec8a3c-1a2a-4e55-9148-955458ca2eb3%2Fqjse5gp.webp%3F1789031992453&amp;w=750&amp;q=75 750w, https://cdn.typeflo.io/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fauth.typeflo.io%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Fposts%2Fpublic%2F6eae6931-f95c-4bcd-b740-e9c3acce8146%2F45ec8a3c-1a2a-4e55-9148-955458ca2eb3%2Fqjse5gp.webp%3F1789031992453&amp;w=828&amp;q=75 828w, https://cdn.typeflo.io/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fauth.typeflo.io%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Fposts%2Fpublic%2F6eae6931-f95c-4bcd-b740-e9c3acce8146%2F45ec8a3c-1a2a-4e55-9148-955458ca2eb3%2Fqjse5gp.webp%3F1789031992453&amp;w=1080&amp;q=75 1080w, https://cdn.typeflo.io/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fauth.typeflo.io%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Fposts%2Fpublic%2F6eae6931-f95c-4bcd-b740-e9c3acce8146%2F45ec8a3c-1a2a-4e55-9148-955458ca2eb3%2Fqjse5gp.webp%3F1789031992453&amp;w=1200&amp;q=75 1200w, https://cdn.typeflo.io/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fauth.typeflo.io%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Fposts%2Fpublic%2F6eae6931-f95c-4bcd-b740-e9c3acce8146%2F45ec8a3c-1a2a-4e55-9148-955458ca2eb3%2Fqjse5gp.webp%3F1789031992453&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75 1920w, https://cdn.typeflo.io/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fauth.typeflo.io%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Fposts%2Fpublic%2F6eae6931-f95c-4bcd-b740-e9c3acce8146%2F45ec8a3c-1a2a-4e55-9148-955458ca2eb3%2Fqjse5gp.webp%3F1789031992453&amp;w=2048&amp;q=75 2048w, https://cdn.typeflo.io/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fauth.typeflo.io%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Fposts%2Fpublic%2F6eae6931-f95c-4bcd-b740-e9c3acce8146%2F45ec8a3c-1a2a-4e55-9148-955458ca2eb3%2Fqjse5gp.webp%3F1789031992453&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75 3840w\" src=\"https://cdn.typeflo.io/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fauth.typeflo.io%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Fposts%2Fpublic%2F6eae6931-f95c-4bcd-b740-e9c3acce8146%2F45ec8a3c-1a2a-4e55-9148-955458ca2eb3%2Fqjse5gp.webp%3F1789031992453&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75\"/></p><h2 id=\"understand-that-you-are-not-every-thought-that-appears-in-your-mind\"> Understand That You Are Not Every Thought That Appears in Your Mind</h2><p>One of the biggest reasons anxiety becomes overwhelming is that we tend to believe every thought that enters the mind. If the mind says, “Something bad is going to happen,” we immediately start reacting as though the event has already happened. If the mind says, “I may fail,” the body begins experiencing the fear of failure before any result has even arrived.</p><p>This is where a deeper understanding of awareness becomes important. The Bhagavad Gita repeatedly explains the importance of mastering the mind rather than becoming controlled by it. When we are completely identified with our thoughts, every thought has the power to disturb us. But when we begin observing those thoughts, we create some distance between ourselves and the mental story.</p><p>This is the essence of <strong>Sakshi Bhav</strong>, or the attitude of the witness. Instead of saying, “I am anxious,” try noticing, “There is anxiety arising in my mind.” Instead of saying, “Everything is going wrong,” recognise that the mind is producing a fearful interpretation of the situation.</p><p>This small shift can be powerful. You are not denying what you feel. You are simply refusing to become completely lost in it.</p><p>If you want to understand <strong>how to reduce anxiety</strong>, start by learning to observe your thoughts before reacting to them. The mind may continue producing fear, but you do not have to follow every fearful thought.</p><div class=\"nc-SectionBecomeAnAuthor w-full rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-neutral-800 dark:border-neutral-700 px-5 py-4 \"><div class=\"custom-cta-section flex flex-col\"><h4 class=\"custom-cta-title font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white text-[19px] leading-snug !m-0\">Design Your Destiny</h4><p class=\"custom-cta-subtitle text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 !mt-1 !mb-0\">Knowing what creates fear, stress and overthinking is only the beginning. Real change begins when awareness becomes action.  Design Your Destiny helps you move towards a more conscious way of living by understanding your inner patterns, observing your mind and applying spiritual wisdom to everyday challenges.  Take the next step towards clarity, awareness and conscious living.</p><a href=\"https://www.udemy.com/course/inner-transformation-masterclass-with-sakshi-shree-hindi/?srsltid=AfmBOoogBhPRKvoviHagsu_eRQISN1B50noJmvEWU2CK-78Bl0MxZ-Yk\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"custom-cta-btn self-start inline-flex items-center px-4 h-9 rounded-lg bg-primary-500 text-white text-sm font-medium hover:bg-primary-600 transition-colors !no-underline mt-3\">Start Your Journey Today!</a>",
