    "slug": "can-women-perform-shraddha-pitru-paksha",
    "oldUrl": "https://sciencedivine.org/blog/can-women-perform-shraddha-pitru-paksha",
    "title": "Can Women Perform Shraddha? Complete Guide for Pitru Paksha",
    "excerpt": "Can women perform Shraddha during Pitru Paksha? Understand Hindu traditions concerning women, daughters and wives performing Shradh, Tarpan and Pind Daan, along with important ritual considerations.",
    "category": "Festivals & Traditions",
    "categorySlug": "festivals-traditions",
    "date": "Sep 10, 2026",
    "datePublished": "2026-09-10T06:23:15.296+00:00",
    "readTime": "2 min read",
    "words": 363,
    "author": {
      "name": "Sakshi Shree",
      "role": "Enlightened Master & Founder, Science Divine",
      "avatar": "https://sciencedivine.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/Sakshi-Shree-Profile-1.webp"
    },
    "image": "/blog/images/can-women-perform-shraddha-pitru-paksha.webp",
    "content": "Pitru Paksha is a sacred period dedicated to remembering ancestors with gratitude, prayer and traditional rituals such as Shraddha, Tarpan and Pind Daan . Yet one question arises frequently in many Hindu families: Can women perform Shraddha? The simple answer is that women can perform Shraddha in many Hindu traditions and circumstances , particularly when they are the appropriate family member to carry forward the ancestral remembrance. However, specific practices concerning who acts as the karta , which mantras are recited and how Tarpan or Pind Daan is performed can differ according to family tradition, region and sampradaya. Traditionally, the eldest son has often been given primary responsibility for ancestral rites. However, this does not mean that every Hindu tradition completely excludes women. Some ritual traditions recognize daughters, wives, mothers, daughters-in-law and other relatives as eligible to perform Shraddha under particular circumstances. Therefore, rather than ask...",
    "contentHtml": "<p>Pitru Paksha is a sacred period dedicated to remembering ancestors with gratitude, prayer and traditional rituals such as <strong>Shraddha, Tarpan and Pind Daan</strong>. Yet one question arises frequently in many Hindu families: <strong>Can women perform Shraddha?</strong></p><p>The simple answer is that <strong>women can perform Shraddha in many Hindu traditions and circumstances</strong>, particularly when they are the appropriate family member to carry forward the ancestral remembrance. However, specific practices concerning who acts as the <em>karta</em>, which mantras are recited and how Tarpan or Pind Daan is performed can differ according to family tradition, region and sampradaya.</p><p>Traditionally, the eldest son has often been given primary responsibility for ancestral rites. However, this does not mean that every Hindu tradition completely excludes women. Some ritual traditions recognize daughters, wives, mothers, daughters-in-law and other relatives as eligible to perform Shraddha under particular circumstances.</p><p>Therefore, rather than asking only <strong>“Can women do Shradh?”</strong>, it is useful to understand the deeper meaning of Shraddha, who may perform it and how different traditions approach women participating in Pitru Paksha rituals.<br/><img alt=\": Woman performing Shraddha rituals by a riverside with pind daan offerings, diya and kalash during Pitru Paksha, with the title “Can Women Perform Shraddha?”\" fetchPriority=\"high\" width=\"1588\" height=\"893\" decoding=\"async\" data-nimg=\"1\" class=\"rounded-lg md:mx-auto lg:mx-auto  xl:mx-auto\" style=\"color:transparent\" sizes=\"100vw\" srcSet=\"https://cdn.typeflo.io/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fauth.typeflo.io%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Fposts%2Fpublic%2F6eae6931-f95c-4bcd-b740-e9c3acce8146%2Fde931322-fe8f-4fc4-8ff7-8f9c7b7e9318%2Fjj3y8lp.webp%3F1789021815686&amp;w=640&amp;q=75 640w, https://cdn.typeflo.io/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fauth.typeflo.io%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Fposts%2Fpublic%2F6eae6931-f95c-4bcd-b740-e9c3acce8146%2Fde931322-fe8f-4fc4-8ff7-8f9c7b7e9318%2Fjj3y8lp.webp%3F1789021815686&amp;w=750&amp;q=75 750w, https://cdn.typeflo.io/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fauth.typeflo.io%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Fposts%2Fpublic%2F6eae6931-f95c-4bcd-b740-e9c3acce8146%2Fde931322-fe8f-4fc4-8ff7-8f9c7b7e9318%2Fjj3y8lp.webp%3F1789021815686&amp;w=828&amp;q=75 828w, https://cdn.typeflo.io/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fauth.typeflo.io%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Fposts%2Fpublic%2F6eae6931-f95c-4bcd-b740-e9c3acce8146%2Fde931322-fe8f-4fc4-8ff7-8f9c7b7e9318%2Fjj3y8lp.webp%3F1789021815686&amp;w=1080&amp;q=75 1080w, https://cdn.typeflo.io/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fauth.typeflo.io%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Fposts%2Fpublic%2F6eae6931-f95c-4bcd-b740-e9c3acce8146%2Fde931322-fe8f-4fc4-8ff7-8f9c7b7e9318%2Fjj3y8lp.webp%3F1789021815686&amp;w=1200&amp;q=75 1200w, https://cdn.typeflo.io/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fauth.typeflo.io%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Fposts%2Fpublic%2F6eae6931-f95c-4bcd-b740-e9c3acce8146%2Fde931322-fe8f-4fc4-8ff7-8f9c7b7e9318%2Fjj3y8lp.webp%3F1789021815686&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75 1920w, https://cdn.typeflo.io/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fauth.typeflo.io%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Fposts%2Fpublic%2F6eae6931-f95c-4bcd-b740-e9c3acce8146%2Fde931322-fe8f-4fc4-8ff7-8f9c7b7e9318%2Fjj3y8lp.webp%3F1789021815686&amp;w=2048&amp;q=75 2048w, https://cdn.typeflo.io/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fauth.typeflo.io%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Fposts%2Fpublic%2F6eae6931-f95c-4bcd-b740-e9c3acce8146%2Fde931322-fe8f-4fc4-8ff7-8f9c7b7e9318%2Fjj3y8lp.webp%3F1789021815686&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75 3840w\" src=\"https://cdn.typeflo.io/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fauth.typeflo.io%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Fposts%2Fpublic%2F6eae6931-f95c-4bcd-b740-e9c3acce8146%2Fde931322-fe8f-4fc4-8ff7-8f9c7b7e9318%2Fjj3y8lp.webp%3F1789021815686&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75\"/></p><h2 id=\"what-is-shraddha\">What Is Shraddha?</h2><p>The word <strong>Shraddha</strong> comes from the idea of performing an action with <em>shraddha</em> like faith, sincerity and reverence.</p><p>Shraddha refers to rituals performed in memory of departed ancestors. During Pitru Paksha, families remember their forefathers and express gratitude for the lineage, values and life they have received.</p><p>Common elements associated with Shraddha may include prayers for ancestors, Tarpan or offerings of water, Pind Daan, food offerings, feeding Brahmins or people in need, charity and remembrance of departed family members.</p><p>The exact procedure can vary considerably across regions and families.</p><p>The deeper purpose of Shraddha is not merely the mechanical performance of a ritual. It represents remembrance, gratitude and the continuing connection between generations.<br/></p><div class=\"nc-SectionBecomeAnAuthor w-full rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-neutral-800 dark:border-neutral-700 px-5 py-4 \"><div class=\"custom-cta-section flex flex-col\"><h4 class=\"custom-cta-title font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white text-[19px] leading-snug !m-0\">Design Your Destiny</h4><p class=\"custom-cta-subtitle text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 !mt-1 !mb-0\">Ancient wisdom is not meant only to be read—it is meant to transform how you think, act and live.  Through Design Your Destiny, discover practical spiritual wisdom that can help you understand your mind, break limiting patterns, make conscious choices and create a more peaceful, purposeful life.  Begin your journey with Design Your Destiny and take charge of the life you are creating.</p><a href=\"https://www.udemy.com/course/inner-transformation-masterclass-with-sakshi-shree-hindi/?srsltid=AfmBOoogBhPRKvoviHagsu_eRQISN1B50noJmvEWU2CK-78Bl0MxZ-Yk\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"custom-cta-btn self-start inline-flex items-center px-4 h-9 rounded-lg bg-primary-500 text-white text-sm font-medium hover:bg-primary-600 transition-colors !no-underline mt-3\">Start Your Journey Today!</a>",
