    "image": "/blog/images/hartalika-teej-2026-fasting-rules.webp",
    "content": "Hartalika Teej is one of the most significant Hindu vrats dedicated to Goddess Parvati and Lord Shiva . Observed on Bhadrapada Shukla Tritiya , the festival represents Goddess Parvati’s unwavering devotion, determination and tapasya to attain Lord Shiva as her husband. In 2026, Hartalika Teej will be observed in India on Monday, September 14, 2026 according to commonly followed Indian Panchang calculations. For Delhi, Tritiya Tithi begins at approximately 7:08 AM on September 13 and ends at 7:06 AM on September 14 . The Pratahkal Hartalika Puja Muhurat in Delhi is approximately 6:05 AM to 7:06 AM . Exact puja timings vary according to location, so devotees should check their local Panchang. Understanding the Hartalika Teej fasting rules 2026 is especially important because the traditional form of this vrat is considered rigorous. Many devotees observe a Nirjala vrat , abstaining from both food and water, while worshipping Shiva and Parvati with devotion. However, spiritual observance s...",
    "contentHtml": "<p>Hartalika Teej is one of the most significant Hindu vrats dedicated to <strong>Goddess Parvati and Lord Shiva</strong>. Observed on <strong>Bhadrapada Shukla Tritiya</strong>, the festival represents Goddess Parvati’s unwavering devotion, determination and tapasya to attain Lord Shiva as her husband.</p><p>In 2026, <strong>Hartalika Teej will be observed in India on Monday, September 14, 2026</strong> according to commonly followed Indian Panchang calculations. For Delhi, Tritiya Tithi begins at approximately <strong>7:08 AM on September 13 and ends at 7:06 AM on September 14</strong>. The Pratahkal Hartalika Puja Muhurat in Delhi is approximately <strong>6:05 AM to 7:06 AM</strong>. Exact puja timings vary according to location, so devotees should check their local Panchang.</p><p>Understanding the <strong>Hartalika Teej fasting rules 2026</strong> is especially important because the traditional form of this vrat is considered rigorous. Many devotees observe a <strong>Nirjala vrat</strong>, abstaining from both food and water, while worshipping Shiva and Parvati with devotion.</p><p>However, spiritual observance should always be balanced with health. Anyone who is pregnant, breastfeeding, unwell, taking regular medication or managing conditions such as diabetes or blood-pressure disorders should seek medical advice before attempting a waterless fast.<br/><img alt=\"Hartalika Teej 2026 fasting rules with a woman performing puja before Lord Shiva and Goddess Parvati, featuring diyas, flowers and a traditional puja thali.\" fetchPriority=\"high\" width=\"1588\" height=\"893\" decoding=\"async\" data-nimg=\"1\" class=\"rounded-lg md:mx-auto lg:mx-auto  xl:mx-auto\" style=\"color:transparent\" sizes=\"100vw\" srcSet=\"https://cdn.typeflo.io/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fauth.typeflo.io%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Fposts%2Fpublic%2F6eae6931-f95c-4bcd-b740-e9c3acce8146%2Fd5db0436-3353-4e0a-a6cf-5f4e24c69f7f%2Fj90t4kc.webp%3F1789020665511&amp;w=640&amp;q=75 640w, https://cdn.typeflo.io/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fauth.typeflo.io%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Fposts%2Fpublic%2F6eae6931-f95c-4bcd-b740-e9c3acce8146%2Fd5db0436-3353-4e0a-a6cf-5f4e24c69f7f%2Fj90t4kc.webp%3F1789020665511&amp;w=750&amp;q=75 750w, https://cdn.typeflo.io/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fauth.typeflo.io%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Fposts%2Fpublic%2F6eae6931-f95c-4bcd-b740-e9c3acce8146%2Fd5db0436-3353-4e0a-a6cf-5f4e24c69f7f%2Fj90t4kc.webp%3F1789020665511&amp;w=828&amp;q=75 828w, https://cdn.typeflo.io/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fauth.typeflo.io%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Fposts%2Fpublic%2F6eae6931-f95c-4bcd-b740-e9c3acce8146%2Fd5db0436-3353-4e0a-a6cf-5f4e24c69f7f%2Fj90t4kc.webp%3F1789020665511&amp;w=1080&amp;q=75 1080w, https://cdn.typeflo.io/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fauth.typeflo.io%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Fposts%2Fpublic%2F6eae6931-f95c-4bcd-b740-e9c3acce8146%2Fd5db0436-3353-4e0a-a6cf-5f4e24c69f7f%2Fj90t4kc.webp%3F1789020665511&amp;w=1200&amp;q=75 1200w, https://cdn.typeflo.io/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fauth.typeflo.io%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Fposts%2Fpublic%2F6eae6931-f95c-4bcd-b740-e9c3acce8146%2Fd5db0436-3353-4e0a-a6cf-5f4e24c69f7f%2Fj90t4kc.webp%3F1789020665511&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75 1920w, https://cdn.typeflo.io/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fauth.typeflo.io%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Fposts%2Fpublic%2F6eae6931-f95c-4bcd-b740-e9c3acce8146%2Fd5db0436-3353-4e0a-a6cf-5f4e24c69f7f%2Fj90t4kc.webp%3F1789020665511&amp;w=2048&amp;q=75 2048w, https://cdn.typeflo.io/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fauth.typeflo.io%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Fposts%2Fpublic%2F6eae6931-f95c-4bcd-b740-e9c3acce8146%2Fd5db0436-3353-4e0a-a6cf-5f4e24c69f7f%2Fj90t4kc.webp%3F1789020665511&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75 3840w\" src=\"https://cdn.typeflo.io/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fauth.typeflo.io%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Fposts%2Fpublic%2F6eae6931-f95c-4bcd-b740-e9c3acce8146%2Fd5db0436-3353-4e0a-a6cf-5f4e24c69f7f%2Fj90t4kc.webp%3F1789020665511&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75\"/></p><h2 id=\"hartalika-teej-2026-date-and-puja-timing\">Hartalika Teej 2026 Date and Puja Timing</h2><p><strong>Hartalika Teej 2026 Date:</strong> Monday, September 14, 2026<br/><strong>Tritiya Tithi Begins:</strong> September 13, around 7:08 AM<br/><strong>Tritiya Tithi Ends:</strong> September 14, around 7:06 AM<br/><strong>Delhi Pratahkal Puja Muhurat:</strong> Approximately 6:05 AM–7:06 AM</p><p>Hartalika Teej falls during the Shukla Paksha Tritiya of the Hindu month of Bhadrapada. Morning is traditionally considered an auspicious period for Hartalika worship. When morning worship is not possible, Shiva-Parvati worship during Pradosh Kaal is also traditionally followed.</p><p>Because sunrise and other Panchang calculations vary geographically, readers outside Delhi should check timings for their own city before performing the puja.<br/></p><div class=\"nc-SectionBecomeAnAuthor w-full rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-neutral-800 dark:border-neutral-700 px-5 py-4 \"><div class=\"custom-cta-section flex flex-col\"><h4 class=\"custom-cta-title font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white text-[19px] leading-snug !m-0\">Design Your Destiny</h4><p class=\"custom-cta-subtitle text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 !mt-1 !mb-0\">Spiritual wisdom is not meant only to be read—it is meant to transform the way you think, choose and live.  Design Your Destiny helps you understand your inner patterns, move beyond limiting beliefs and bring greater awareness into everyday life.  Begin your journey with Design Your Destiny and take conscious steps towards the life you truly wish to create.</p><a href=\"https://www.udemy.com/course/inner-transformation-masterclass-with-sakshi-shree-hindi/?srsltid=AfmBOoogBhPRKvoviHagsu_eRQISN1B50noJmvEWU2CK-78Bl0MxZ-Yk\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"custom-cta-btn self-start inline-flex items-center px-4 h-9 rounded-lg bg-primary-500 text-white text-sm font-medium hover:bg-primary-600 transition-colors !no-underline mt-3\">Start Your Journey Today!</a>",
