    "contentHtml": "<p>Parsva Ekadashi is one of the significant Ekadashi vrats dedicated to Lord Vishnu. Observed during the Shukla Paksha of the Bhadrapada month, this sacred day is associated with devotion, fasting, self-discipline and spiritual reflection.</p><p>Devotees searching for the <strong>Parsva Ekadashi 2026 date</strong>, <strong>Parsva Ekadashi 2026 parana time</strong>, <strong>Parsva Ekadashi vrat katha</strong>, and <strong>Parsva Ekadashi puja vidhi</strong> observe the occasion by fasting, worshipping Lord Vishnu, chanting His names and engaging in devotional practices.</p><p>Parsva Ekadashi is also popularly known as <strong>Parshva Ekadashi, Parivartini Ekadashi, Padma Ekadashi and Vamana Ekadashi</strong> in different traditions and regions.</p><p>The name <em>Parivartini</em> is associated with the traditional belief that Lord Vishnu, who rests in Yoga Nidra during Chaturmas, changes His sleeping position on this Ekadashi.</p><p>In 2026, Parsva Ekadashi will be observed on <strong>Tuesday, September 22, 2026</strong>. For New Delhi, the Ekadashi Tithi begins at <strong>8:00 PM on September 21</strong> and ends at <strong>9:43 PM on September 22</strong>.<br/><img alt=\"Parsva Ekadashi 2026 banner featuring Lord Vishnu with glowing diyas and the title “Date, Time, Parana, Vrat Katha &amp; Puja Vidhi.”\" fetchPriority=\"high\" width=\"1588\" height=\"893\" decoding=\"async\" data-nimg=\"1\" class=\"rounded-lg md:mx-auto lg:mx-auto  xl:mx-auto\" style=\"color:transparent\" sizes=\"100vw\" srcSet=\"https://cdn.typeflo.io/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fauth.typeflo.io%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Fposts%2Fpublic%2F6eae6931-f95c-4bcd-b740-e9c3acce8146%2Fe80f09f7-05e4-4626-955e-42295eb44e18%2Fr0hc54u.webp%3F1788262456131&amp;w=640&amp;q=75 640w, https://cdn.typeflo.io/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fauth.typeflo.io%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Fposts%2Fpublic%2F6eae6931-f95c-4bcd-b740-e9c3acce8146%2Fe80f09f7-05e4-4626-955e-42295eb44e18%2Fr0hc54u.webp%3F1788262456131&amp;w=750&amp;q=75 750w, https://cdn.typeflo.io/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fauth.typeflo.io%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Fposts%2Fpublic%2F6eae6931-f95c-4bcd-b740-e9c3acce8146%2Fe80f09f7-05e4-4626-955e-42295eb44e18%2Fr0hc54u.webp%3F1788262456131&amp;w=828&amp;q=75 828w, https://cdn.typeflo.io/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fauth.typeflo.io%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Fposts%2Fpublic%2F6eae6931-f95c-4bcd-b740-e9c3acce8146%2Fe80f09f7-05e4-4626-955e-42295eb44e18%2Fr0hc54u.webp%3F1788262456131&amp;w=1080&amp;q=75 1080w, https://cdn.typeflo.io/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fauth.typeflo.io%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Fposts%2Fpublic%2F6eae6931-f95c-4bcd-b740-e9c3acce8146%2Fe80f09f7-05e4-4626-955e-42295eb44e18%2Fr0hc54u.webp%3F1788262456131&amp;w=1200&amp;q=75 1200w, https://cdn.typeflo.io/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fauth.typeflo.io%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Fposts%2Fpublic%2F6eae6931-f95c-4bcd-b740-e9c3acce8146%2Fe80f09f7-05e4-4626-955e-42295eb44e18%2Fr0hc54u.webp%3F1788262456131&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75 1920w, https://cdn.typeflo.io/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fauth.typeflo.io%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Fposts%2Fpublic%2F6eae6931-f95c-4bcd-b740-e9c3acce8146%2Fe80f09f7-05e4-4626-955e-42295eb44e18%2Fr0hc54u.webp%3F1788262456131&amp;w=2048&amp;q=75 2048w, https://cdn.typeflo.io/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fauth.typeflo.io%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Fposts%2Fpublic%2F6eae6931-f95c-4bcd-b740-e9c3acce8146%2Fe80f09f7-05e4-4626-955e-42295eb44e18%2Fr0hc54u.webp%3F1788262456131&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75 3840w\" src=\"https://cdn.typeflo.io/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fauth.typeflo.io%2Fstorage%2Fv1%2Fobject%2Fpublic%2Fposts%2Fpublic%2F6eae6931-f95c-4bcd-b740-e9c3acce8146%2Fe80f09f7-05e4-4626-955e-42295eb44e18%2Fr0hc54u.webp%3F1788262456131&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75\"/></p><h2 id=\"parsva-ekadashi-2026-date-and-time\">Parsva Ekadashi 2026 Date and Time</h2><p>The <strong>Parsva Ekadashi 2026 date</strong> is:</p><p><strong>Tuesday, September 22, 2026</strong></p><h3 id=\"parsva-ekadashi-2026-tithi\">Parsva Ekadashi 2026 Tithi</h3><p>For New Delhi:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Ekadashi Tithi Begins:</strong> September 21, 2026 at 8:00 PM</p></li><li><p><strong>Ekadashi Tithi Ends:</strong> September 22, 2026 at 9:43 PM</p></li><li><p><strong>Parsva Ekadashi Vrat:</strong> September 22, 2026</p></li><li><p><strong>Parana:</strong> September 23, 2026</p></li></ul><p>The timing can vary slightly depending on geographical location. Devotees should therefore check their local Panchang before performing Parana or time-sensitive rituals.</p><p>Parsva Ekadashi occurs on the <strong>Shukla Paksha Ekadashi of Bhadrapada month</strong> according to the traditional Hindu lunar calendar.<br/></p><div class=\"nc-SectionBecomeAnAuthor w-full rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-neutral-800 dark:border-neutral-700 px-5 py-4 \"><div class=\"custom-cta-section flex flex-col\"><h4 class=\"custom-cta-title font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white text-[19px] leading-snug !m-0\">Design Your Destiny</h4><p class=\"custom-cta-subtitle text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400 !mt-1 !mb-0\">Explore Design Your Destiny, a transformative journey designed to help you understand your inner patterns, develop greater awareness and consciously shape the direction of your life.  Start your journey toward designing your destiny today.</p><a href=\"https://www.udemy.com/course/inner-transformation-masterclass-with-sakshi-shree-hindi/?srsltid=AfmBOoogBhPRKvoviHagsu_eRQISN1B50noJmvEWU2CK-78Bl0MxZ-Yk\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"custom-cta-btn self-start inline-flex items-center px-4 h-9 rounded-lg bg-primary-500 text-white text-sm font-medium hover:bg-primary-600 transition-colors !no-underline mt-3\">Start Your Journey Today!</a>",
